{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists taking care of you. You were admitted for a flare of your Crohn’s disease. Can you tell me about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it started a couple nights ago. I was having about 12 bowel movements a day, which is my usual, but then suddenly it got worse. I was up every half hour all night with watery diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned pain—where is it located?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Mainly in the left upper side. It gets worse when I have to go. Feels like a squeezing, crampy pain. I also had a fever at home and felt really weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for that. We gave you IV steroids in the ER to help calm the inflammation. We’ve also started IV fluids because you’ve been losing a lot through diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I took more prednisone at home—up to 35 mg—but it didn’t help much. And lomotil didn’t stop the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. When flares are this severe, oral meds often aren’t enough. We’re giving you IV methylprednisolone now, which is stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Are we checking for infections? I didn’t eat anything strange."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, excellent question. We sent stool tests for C. diff, parasites, and common bacteria like Salmonella. So far, all negative. That supports this being a flare, not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. But the pain is still pretty bad. Can I get something for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given IV Dilaudid, and you’re on a PCA pump so you can control it. We’re being careful because narcotics can slow the gut, but we want you comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling kind of dizzy too. Is that from the diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2178-01-06 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely from dehydration. Your blood pressure was low when you came in. The IV fluids should help with that over the next day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2178-01-06 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray this afternoon. No signs of blockage or free air, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2178-01-06 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I still feel bloated. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2178-01-06 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, inflammation can cause that. We’re keeping you NPO—no food—for now to let your bowel rest. We’ll start clear liquids once things settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2178-01-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your white count is elevated, which fits with inflammation. Your kidney function was a bit off—creatinine up to 1.3—but that’s improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2178-01-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? My kidneys have been an issue before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2178-01-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s acute and likely due to dehydration. It’s already coming down. We’ll keep monitoring, but no long-term damage expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2178-01-07 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really anxious. The steroids make me feel wired, especially at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2178-01-07 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. We’ve consulted Psychiatry. They recommend low-dose Seroquel at night to help with sleep and anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2178-01-07 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. I just want to feel normal again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2178-01-08 02:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did another X-ray early this morning. There’s some new dilation in the small bowel, especially on the left side. Could be a partial obstruction from inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2178-01-08 02:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2178-01-08 02:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s concerning, but not an emergency. We’re not seeing signs of perforation. We’ll do a CT scan today to get a better look."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2178-01-08 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT is back. Good news—no abscess, perforation, or blockage. The area around your anastomosis is thickened, but it’s not worse than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2178-01-08 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s just inflammation, not a new problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2178-01-08 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your Crohn’s is active there, but no surgical issue. We also noticed your spleen is larger than last time. We’ll follow that up with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2178-01-08 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2178-01-08 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not immediately, but it needs monitoring. It can happen with chronic inflammation. Your PCP and GI will keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2178-01-09 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting you on IV Imuran—azathioprine. It’s a steroid-sparing agent to help get you off high-dose prednisone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2178-01-09 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried that before, right? I think my kidneys didn’t like it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2178-01-09 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but that was years ago. We’ll start low and monitor your labs closely. It’s important for long-term control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2178-01-09 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try some food? I’m tired of just IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2178-01-09 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can try clear liquids. But go slow—your gut’s been resting. If you push too fast, it could flare again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2178-01-09 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had some broth and then my pain got worse. And I’ve had more bowel movements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2178-01-09 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we were worried about. We’ll hold off on advancing your diet for now. Bowel rest is still important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2178-01-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your bowel movements have decreased—from over 20 at home to about 6 per day. That’s progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2178-01-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I feel stuck here. I think I can manage better at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2178-01-10 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but we’re not quite ready to discharge. We need your pain and diarrhea more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been thinking—I want to go home today. I know it’s against advice, but I’ll follow up with my GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. But leaving AMA means the flare could worsen—risk of dehydration, hospitalization, or complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know the risks. I just need to be at home. I’ll take my meds and come back if it gets bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll discharge you with a plan. You’ll take prednisone 40 mg daily, Imuran 75 mg, Protonix, and opium tincture for diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the Seroquel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one tablet twice a day as needed, especially at night. And loperamide if the opium isn’t available yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GI in one week, primary care in two. We’ve scheduled both. Call us if pain, fever, or bloody stools return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I’ll stay on top of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2178-01-11 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be here if you need us. Take care, and good luck at home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2178-01-06 11:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2178-01-11 16:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a male with a history of Crohn’s disease status post subtotal colectomy, was admitted for an acute exacerbation characterized by over 20 daily watery bowel movements, left upper quadrant abdominal pain, and fevers. He was started on IV methylprednisolone and IV fluids for dehydration, which improved his creatinine from 1.3 to 1.0. Abdominal imaging showed stable bowel wall thickening at the anastomosis site and new splenomegaly. A repeat X-ray suggested possible partial obstruction, but CT ruled out perforation or abscess. Stool studies were negative for infection. The patient developed steroid-induced anxiety, managed with Seroquel. He insisted on discharge against medical advice on hospital day 5, after showing some improvement with reduced bowel movements. He was discharged on prednisone, azathioprine, Protonix, opium tincture, and Seroquel, with follow-up arranged in GI and primary care clinics.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of large intestine",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Abdominal pain, left upper quadrant",
      "Unspecified adjustment reaction",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Adrenal cortical steroids causing adverse effects in therapeutic use"
    ]
  }
}
